{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChJv7EqAhGMHvbpSh92HF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RPH7NGHhAjfYEZ9F4YxV2W","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/nx/03lmtb354_bblp90rfd257xr0000gn/T/mergejudge-matplotlib-18869-claude-e2e-r2-run; cat > doc/users/next_whats_new/version_info.rst <<'EOF'\nVersion information\n-------------------\nIn addition to the string ``__version__``, there is now a namedtuple\n``__version_info__`` as well, which is modelled after `sys.version_info`_.\nIts primary use is safely comparing version information, e.g.\n``if __version_info__ >= (3, 4, 2)``.\n\n.. _sys.version_info: https://docs.python.org/3/library/sys.html#sys.version_info\nEOF\ngit status --short"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":534,"cache_read_input_tokens":23313,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":534},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5a54054-32b5-4b23-b0fe-ed2b3a2d383e","uuid":"d938f5f1-ad20-4072-aa58-1cd37b037152","timestamp":"2026-11-23T00:30:55.884Z","request_id":"req_011ChJv7EfVqC7hf7FXbNPPf"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RPH7NGHhAjfYEZ9F4YxV2W","type":"tool_result","content":" M lib/matplotlib/__init__.py\n?? doc/users/next_whats_new/version_info.rst","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5a54054-32b5-4b23-b0fe-ed2b3a2d383e","uuid":"d9df19c6-fd79-4a30-980f-5e2c640d8b61","timestamp":"2026-11-23T00:30:56.070Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":" M lib/matplotlib/__init__.py\n?? doc/users/next_whats_new/version_info.rst","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/nx/03lmtb354_bblp90rfd257xr0000gn/T/mergejudge-matplotlib-18869-claude-e2e-r2-run/doc/users/next_whats_new/version_info.rst","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":15,"newStart":1,"newLines":8,"lines":[" Version information"," -------------------","-We switched to the `release-branch-semver`_ version scheme. This only affects,","-the version information for development builds. Their version number now","-describes the targeted release, i.e. 3.5.0.dev820+g6768ef8c4c is 820 commits","-after the previous release and is scheduled to be officially released as 3.5.0","-later.","-"," In addition to the string ``__version__``, there is now a namedtuple"," ``__version_info__`` as well, which is modelled after `sys.version_info`_."," Its primary use is safely comparing version information, e.g."," ``if __version_info__ >= (3, 4, 2)``."," ","-.. _release-branch-semver: https://github.com/pypa/setuptools_scm#version-number-construction"," .. _sys.version_info: https://docs.python.org/3/library/sys.html#sys.version_info"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/private/var/folders/nx/03lmtb354_bblp90rfd257xr0000gn/T/mergejudge-matplotlib-18869-claude-e2e-r2-run/doc/users/next_whats_new/version_info.rst"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RPH7NGHhAjfYEZ9F4YxV2W","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChJv7V7eXN1jFM35HiBJH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Matplotlib now has `matplotlib.__version_info__`, a named tuple shaped like `sys.version_info`. It can be compared directly with tuples, e.g. `matplotlib.__version_info__ >= (3, 4, 2)`. The 4 tests in `test_matplotlib.py` pass, and I checked the parser by hand on four sample version strings. I didn't add a new test for it.\n\nThe change is in `lib/matplotlib/__init__.py`:\n- **Parsing:** a new `_parse_to_version_info()` turns a version string into the tuple (major, minor, micro, release level, serial). Results:\n  - `3.5.0` → `(3, 5, 0, 'final', 0)`\n  - `3.5.0rc2` → `(3, 5, 0, 'candidate', 2)`\n  - `3.5.0.dev820+g…` → `(3, 5, 0, 'alpha', 820)`\n  - `3.5.0.post820+g…` → `(3, 5, 1, 'alpha', 820)`. This one is a guess: I assumed a post-release build means work toward the next micro release.\n- **Lookup:** I moved the existing logic that works out the version string into a helper, `_get_version()`. The module's `__getattr__` now handles both `__version__` and `__version_info__` and caches the two together the first time either is asked for.\n\nI also added a short what's-new entry at `doc/users/next_whats_new/version_info.rst`.\n\n**Decision for you:** I went with the tuple rather than a `LooseVersion` object. The issue says the tuple is the more common convention, and `LooseVersion` is deprecated in recent Python. If you'd rather expose a comparable version object, the parsed `packaging` version is already available and could be returned instead."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":361,"cache_read_input_tokens":23847,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":361},"output_tokens":585,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5a54054-32b5-4b23-b0fe-ed2b3a2d383e","uuid":"d50304e1-9bfa-4775-9f20-13fa7c3aa56d","timestamp":"2026-11-23T00:31:02.179Z","request_id":"req_011ChJv7UyiQVGzepecy5CJ3"}
